{
  "body": {
    "content": [
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Cơm tấm is a plate of ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "broken rice ",
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "com-tam-rice"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "topped with grilled pork, a fried egg, and a bowl of dipping sauce. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Regular jasmine rice works well if broken rice is hard to find. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "This recipe serves 4.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The pork needs at least an hour to marinate. The sweet and salty glaze is what gives the grilled meat its caramelised crust.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What you need",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "pork-shoulder",
              "amount": 600,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "cut into 1 cm thick steaks",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "pork"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "fish-sauce",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "caster-sugar",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "garlic",
              "amount": 4,
              "unit": "cloves",
              "prepNote": "minced",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "shallots",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "minced",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "sesame-oil",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "jasmine-rice",
              "amount": 300,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "rice"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "eggs",
              "amount": 4,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "to serve"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "radish",
              "amount": 100,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "cut into matchsticks",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "pickles"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "carrot",
              "amount": 100,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "cut into matchsticks",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "pickles"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "lime",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "pickles and sauce"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "vegetable-oil",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Method",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Mix the fish sauce, sugar, garlic, shallots, and sesame oil. Add the pork steaks and turn to coat. Cover and refrigerate for at least 1 hour.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Toss the daikon and carrot with a pinch of seasoning and the lime juice. Add 1 tsp sugar and leave to pickle for 30 minutes.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Make the ",
                    "type": "text"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "nước mắm chấm ",
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "nuoc-mam-cham"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "by mixing 2 tbsp fish sauce, 1 tbsp sugar, 2 tbsp lime juice, and 4 tbsp warm water with a little minced garlic and chilli.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Cook the rice according to the packet instructions. Keep warm.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Heat a griddle pan to high. Remove the pork from the marinade and cook for 3 to 4 minutes per side until charred and cooked through. Rest for 5 minutes, then slice.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Fry the eggs in the vegetable oil over medium heat until the whites are set and the yolks are still runny.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Serve the rice on plates. Top with sliced pork, a fried egg, and a pile of pickled vegetables. Pour the dipping sauce into a small bowl alongside.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          }
        ],
        "type": "orderedList"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Marinate for at least 1 hour, ideally overnight. The fish sauce and sugar need time to penetrate the meat.",
              "cause": "The marinade time was too short.",
              "symptom": "The pork is dry and lacks flavour."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Pound the pork steaks to an even 8 mm thickness before marinating. Thinner steaks cook through quickly on high heat.",
              "cause": "The steaks are too thick for high-heat cooking.",
              "symptom": "The pork burns before it is cooked through."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Add more warm water and a little more sugar and lime juice to balance. The sauce should taste bright and lightly savoury.",
              "cause": "Too much fish sauce relative to water was used.",
              "symptom": "The dipping sauce is too salty."
            }
          }
        ],
        "type": "troubleshooter"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Where this dish lives",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Cơm tấm comes from Ho Chi Minh City in southern Vietnam. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "It was originally eaten by the working class and sold from early morning by street vendors. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "The broken rice was cheap because it was the grain left over after milling. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Today cơm tấm restaurants are open around the clock across the south. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "It is the dish most Saigonese people call their everyday food.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      }
    ],
    "type": "doc"
  },
  "glossaryTerms": [
    {
      "definition": "Broken rice grains that are shorter and more fragile than whole grains. They cook a little softer than regular rice and absorb the flavours of the toppings well.",
      "term": "Cơm tấm",
      "slug": "com-tam-rice"
    },
    {
      "definition": "A Vietnamese dipping sauce made from fish sauce, sugar, lime juice, garlic, and chilli. The essential condiment for cơm tấm.",
      "term": "Nước mắm chấm",
      "slug": "nuoc-mam-cham"
    }
  ],
